@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+---
+type: decision
+status: active
+updated: 2026-11-03
+sources: [.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md, .harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md, commits 4d9b627 3556e27 0be020e dc6668d 9b80c9d, 0005, 0010, 0011]
+verified_by: tests/gate.test.sh (incl. tests/gate-denied.list)
+---
+# 0012: Gate shrink: trim, keep the path helpers and the Bash allowlist
+
+**Context.** Prune step 5 ([0011](0011-single-runner-headless.md)) was to shrink the conductor gate. The analyst plan (`.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md`) measured a 552-line gate with ~410 checks, and replayed 881 real conductor Bash calls from 8 transcripts (2026-10-18..28): 754 allowed, 127 denied (106 of them from two ungated daemon-env sessions). Never used: `git show --stat`; `herdr status`, `pane list|layout`, `workspace|tab list`; `gh issue|run|repo|auth|browse`, `pr status`; jq as a pipe consumer (0 allowed). Chaining used an unquoted `;` in 5.8% of allowed calls, pipes and `2>&1` never. An interactive spike of native subagents instead of the runner (B′, `.harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md`) was rejected on 2026-11-03: subagents die when the conductor exits ("1 local agent couldn't be moved and was stopped"), so the headless runner of [0007](0007-headless-runner-pilot.md) stays, and so does the gate.
+
+**Decision.** Trim the gate to observed use and keep its shape:
+- Removed (earlier commits 3556e27, 4d9b627, 0be020e; verified again in this step): jq handling, `git_branch_ok` (now one regex: `git branch` plus any of `-a -r -v --show-current`), `git show`, all `herdr` except `pane get|current`, all `gh` except `pr create|view|list|checks|comment|edit|merge`, the segment splitter (one-command scanner instead), the Agent/Workflow/Monitor/NotebookEdit deny cases and the `mcp__filesystem__*` block (no such server is configured; `disallowedTools` in `claude/agents/conductor.md` removes the four native tools), and the hook matcher is `Edit|Write|Read|Grep|Glob|Bash`.
+- This step: the `--via` no-op arm is gone (a stale `--via` is now a usage error, exit 1, dc6668d); the policy tables (messages, `BASH_ALLOW`, `GH_ALLOW`, `GIT_DENY*`) sit in one labelled block at the top (9b80c9d); `tests/gate.test.sh` has one check per form under "You may run directly" in `conductor.md`.
+- Kept: the path helpers (`rel`/`physrel`/`physical`/`readable`/`writable`, raw-stream block) and the Bash allowlist with its `cat`/`ls`/`gh --body-file` argument checks. They are what stops `Read bin/harness`, `..`, symlinks out of `docs/`, and `.harness/log/*.jsonl` (raw worker streams, [0007](0007-headless-runner-pilot.md)); each has a regression test and a past review fix behind it.
+- Rejected, option f ("permissions rules" instead of a script): rules in user-scope `settings.json` bind workers too, so the implementer would lose the tools it needs; the gate's `agent_type` keying is what separates the conductor from workers ([0005](0005-gate-only-inside-herdr.md), [0010](0010-herdr-optional-gate-by-checkout.md)).
+
+**Status.** Active. `tests/gate-denied.list` (deny probes plus 5 controls) must stay green through any gate change.
+
+**Consequences.** The gate went from 552 lines (plan baseline) to 513 before this step and 518 after (a header on the policy block); the expected ≤50-line gate of the original critique is not reachable while the path checks stay. This step removes no behaviour from the gate, because the earlier gate commits had already applied options b-d. Supersedes the 4b consequence in 0005 (permissions-rules gate). Adding a command to the allowlist needs a usage reason and a regression probe.
